{
  "concept": "A change of variables T(u,v) = (x(u,v), y(u,v)) maps a small rectangle S in the uv-plane to a curved region R in the xy-plane, and the Jacobian determinant is the local factor by which that map stretches area.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Left panel: uv-plane with horizontal u-axis and vertical v-axis, arrowheads and labels 'u' and 'v'",
    "Left panel: two vertical blue grid lines labeled 'u = u\u2080' and 'u = u\u2080 + \u0394u', extending beyond the rectangle",
    "Left panel: two horizontal blue grid lines labeled 'v = v\u2080' and 'v = v\u2080 + \u0394v', extending beyond the rectangle",
    "Left panel: shaded pale-blue rectangle S formed by those four lines, labeled 'S' at its center",
    "Left panel: four blue corner dots at the rectangle vertices, corner label '(u\u2080, v\u2080)' at the lower-left dot",
    "Left panel: side-length labels '\u0394u' below the bottom edge and '\u0394v' to the right of the right edge",
    "Center: large curved tan/cream arrow with grey outline pointing from left panel to right panel, labeled 'T'",
    "Right panel: xy-plane with horizontal x-axis and vertical y-axis, arrowheads and labels 'x' and 'y'",
    "Right panel: four blue curves, the images of the four boundary lines, each extending past the region, labeled 'Image of u = u\u2080', 'Image of u = u\u2080 + \u0394u', 'Image of v = v\u2080', 'Image of v = v\u2080 + \u0394v'",
    "Right panel: shaded pale-blue curved quadrilateral R bounded by those curves, labeled 'R' at its center",
    "Right panel: four image corner dots corresponding to the rectangle's corners",
    "Optional overlay: tangent vectors (\u2202x/\u2202u, \u2202y/\u2202u)\u0394u and (\u2202x/\u2202v, \u2202y/\u2202v)\u0394v at the image of (u\u2080, v\u2080) with the dashed parallelogram they span",
    "Readout box: area(S) = \u0394u\u00b7\u0394v, area(R) \u2248 |J|\u00b7\u0394u\u00b7\u0394v, and the numeric ratio area(R)/area(S) compared with |\u2202(x,y)/\u2202(u,v)| at (u\u2080, v\u2080)"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "transformation",
      "type": "equation_input",
      "teaches": "The shape of R is entirely dictated by the formulas for x(u,v) and y(u,v); changing them restretches and re-curves the image of the same fixed rectangle.",
      "label": "Transformation T(u,v)",
      "fields": [
        {
          "id": "xuv",
          "label": "x(u,v) =",
          "default": "u*cos(v)",
          "variables": ["u", "v"],
          "domain": [0, 3],
          "role": "x-component of the map"
        },
        {
          "id": "yuv",
          "label": "y(u,v) =",
          "default": "u*sin(v)",
          "variables": ["u", "v"],
          "domain": [0, 3],
          "role": "y-component of the map"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dragCorner",
      "type": "drag",
      "teaches": "Moving the rectangle to a different (u\u2080, v\u2080) or resizing it shows that the same map distorts area differently at different points \u2014 the stretching factor is local, not global.",
      "teaches_note": "drag the lower-left corner to reposition S, drag the upper-right corner to resize it"
    },
    {
      "id": "shrink",
      "type": "slider",
      "teaches": "As \u0394u and \u0394v shrink, the curved sides of R straighten and the area ratio area(R)/area(S) converges to the Jacobian determinant at (u\u2080, v\u2080).",
      "label": "Cell size \u0394u = \u0394v",
      "range": [0.05, 1.2, 0.05],
      "default": 0.8
    },
    {
      "id": "showJacobian",
      "type": "toggle",
      "teaches": "The curved image is well approximated by the parallelogram spanned by the tangent vectors T_u\u0394u and T_v\u0394v, whose area is exactly |J|\u0394u\u0394v.",
      "label": "Tangent-vector parallelogram & area readout",
      "default": false
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "A rectangle and its image",
      "narration": "The pale rectangle S in the uv-plane is built from two u-lines and two v-lines. Under T(u,v) = (u cos v, u sin v) those four straight lines become four curves, and S becomes the curved region R.",
      "state": { "shrink": 0.8, "showJacobian": false }
    },
    {
      "title": "Which curve came from which line",
      "narration": "Each edge keeps its identity: the line u = u\u2080 maps to a circular arc, the line v = v\u2080 maps to a ray. Drag a corner of S and watch every image curve follow.",
      "state": { "shrink": 0.8, "showJacobian": false }
    },
    {
      "title": "The Jacobian as a stretch factor",
      "narration": "Turn on the tangent vectors. The parallelogram they span hugs R, and its area is |\u2202(x,y)/\u2202(u,v)| times the area \u0394u\u0394v of S.",
      "state": { "shrink": 0.8, "showJacobian": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "Shrink the cell",
      "narration": "Reduce \u0394u and \u0394v. The curved sides flatten, R becomes indistinguishable from the parallelogram, and the ratio area(R)/area(S) locks onto the Jacobian value at (u\u2080, v\u2080).",
      "state": { "shrink": 0.1, "showJacobian": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "Change the map",
      "narration": "Edit x(u,v) and y(u,v) \u2014 try x = u\u00b2 \u2212 v\u00b2, y = 2uv. The rectangle never moves, but R and the local stretch factor change completely.",
      "state": { "shrink": 0.4, "showJacobian": true }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "dA in the xy-plane is not du dv: a change of variables bends a rectangle into a curved patch whose area is |\u2202(x,y)/\u2202(u,v)| du dv, and that Jacobian factor is just the local area-stretch of the map.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Two side-by-side panels on white. Both panels have thin black axes with arrowheads, labeled u/v on the left and x/y on the right, origin near the lower-left of each panel. Left panel: four medium-thick cyan-blue straight lines (two vertical, two horizontal) extending noticeably past their intersections; the enclosed rectangle is filled pale steel-blue with a thin border; solid blue dots at the four intersections; serif italic math labels 'u = u\u2080', 'u = u\u2080 + \u0394u' above the vertical lines, 'v = v\u2080', 'v = v\u2080 + \u0394v' to the right of the horizontal lines, '(u\u2080, v\u2080)' below-left of the lower-left dot, '\u0394u' under the bottom edge, '\u0394v' beside the right edge, italic 'S' centered in the shaded rectangle. Between panels: a broad, gently curved block arrow sweeping left-to-right, cream/tan fill with grey outline, drawn with a slight upward bow. Right panel: the same cyan blue used for four smooth curves forming a bulging curved quadrilateral (looks like a distorted parallelogram with convex top and concave-ish left side); each curve overshoots the corner region; the interior is filled the same pale steel-blue with italic 'R' centered; text labels 'Image of u = u\u2080' upper-left, 'Image of u = u\u2080 + \u0394u' upper-right, 'Image of v = v\u2080 + \u0394v' middle-right, 'Image of v = v\u2080' lower-right, each placed at the free end of its curve. When the Jacobian overlay is on, draw two arrows in a contrasting color (orange/red) from the image of (u\u2080,v\u2080) along the two image curves, plus a dashed parallelogram, and a small readout panel giving \u0394u, \u0394v, area(S), area(R), their ratio, and |J| at (u\u2080,v\u2080). Show inline parse errors in red under the offending equation field and keep the last valid curve drawn."
}

